{"name":"Soft Colonial Wanderlust","title":"Soft Colonial Wanderlust","revision":234114,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Soft_Colonial_Wanderlust","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"It differs from other Victorian-inspired aesthetics like Steampunk due to its whimsical and ironic tone and themes of expedition and colonization."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Soft Colonial Wanderlust is inspired by imagery from the Victorian and pre-WWII eras. The aesthetic often uses cut-out 2D figures, engraved illustrations, circus fonts, and muted colors to create an old vintage look. Many motifs include mustaches, suits, top hats, typewriters, phonographs, lightbulbs, and technology of the decade that's on the verge of modernity being used today, but not exactly steampunk like Rube-Goldberg machines."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Exploration is a major theme of the aesthetic since it is influenced by Jules Verne's works, which feature characters going on expeditions to other lands. Many visuals would have characters using old-fashioned forms of transportation like airplanes, boats and hot air balloons. Maps are a common visual as well as tools commonly used for exploration like compasses and binoculars."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Games"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bioshock Infinite"},{"kind":"list","text":"Myst series"},{"kind":"list","text":"Maquette"},{"kind":"list","text":"What Remains of Edith Finch"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Room game series"},{"kind":"list","text":"Adventures of Bertram Fiddle"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rusty Lake"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sunless Skies: Sovereign Edition"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sunless Seas"},{"kind":"list","text":"Valkyria Chronicles"},{"kind":"list","text":"Spiritfarer"},{"kind":"list","text":"Professor Layton game series"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Misadventures of P.B. Winterbottom"},{"kind":"heading","text":"TV Shows and Movies"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Media are included here primarily based on visuals. They commonly adhere to worldbuilding convention of different genres such as \"Gaslight Fantasy\", Steampunk or Dieselpunk."},{"kind":"list","text":"The Adventures of Baron Munchausen (1988)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Back to the Future Part III (1993)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wild Wild West (1999)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The League of Extraordinary Gentlemen (2003)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lemony Snicket's A Series of Unfortunate Events (2004)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Around the World in 80 Days (2004)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pan's Labyrinth (2006)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Illusionist (2006)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Golden Compass (2007)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Marvelous Misadventures of Flapjack (2008-2010)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Imaginarium of Doctor Parnassus (2009)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sherlock Holmes series by Guy Ritchie (2009-2011)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Alice in Wonderland series (2010-2016)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hugo (2011)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Adventures of Tintin (2011)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jack and the Cuckoo-Clock Heart (2013)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Over the Garden Wall (2014)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Miss Peregrine's Home for Peculiar Children (2016)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Greatest Showman (2017)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Aeronauts (2019)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Enola Holmes (2022)"},{"kind":"list","text":"1899 (2022)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Nautilus (2024)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Books"},{"kind":"list","text":"A Series of Unfortunate Events by Lemony Snicket"},{"kind":"list","text":"English Passengers by Matthew Kneale"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Court of the Air by Stephen Hunt"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Glass Town Game by Catherynne M. Valente"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Bedlam Stacks by Natasha Pulley"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Scar by Chine Mieville"},{"kind":"list","text":"Washington Black by Esi Edugyan"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Board Games"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ticket to Ride Europe"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Podcasts"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Orbiting Human Circus (of the Air) (2016)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Music"},{"kind":"list","text":"Parov Stellar"},{"kind":"list","text":"Panic! at the Disco"},{"kind":"list","text":"Arcade Fire"},{"kind":"list","text":"Neutral Milk Hotel"},{"kind":"list","text":"FUN."},{"kind":"list","text":"Tally Hall"},{"kind":"list","text":"Erasure"},{"kind":"list","text":"Enya"},{"kind":"list","text":"Beirut"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Creams"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Kettering Vampires"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Decemberists"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/3b/Tao_of_the_dead.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20260102045559","caption":"Tao of the dead","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Tao_of_the_dead.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0922-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/4b/62cac6398bdd0ba7df7f4107932011b3.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240707205906","caption":"Banana Republic catalogue (1980s)","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:62cac6398bdd0ba7df7f4107932011b3.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0922-2.webp","localAvailable":true}]}